Fire of Love is a documentary film directed by Sara Dosa.

3
00:23:15,000 --> 00:23:21,000
A doomed love triangle between intrepid French scientists Katia
and Maurice Krafft, and their beloved volcanoes.

4
00:31:00,000 --> 00:31:06,000
Katia Conrad Krafft (voice), played by Alka Balbir.

5
00:38:45,000 --> 00:38:51,000
Maurice Krafft (voice), played by Guillaume Tremblay.

6
00:46:30,000 --> 00:46:36,000
Narrator (voice), played by Miranda July.

7
00:54:15,000 --> 00:54:21,000
Fire of Love is a 2022 independent documentary film about the lives
and careers of volcanologists Katia and Maurice Krafft.

8
01:02:00,000 --> 01:02:06,000
Directed, written, and produced by Sara Dosa, the film had its world premiere at the 2022 Sundance
Film Festival on January 20, 2022, where it won the Jonathan Oppenheim Editing Award.

9
01:09:45,000 --> 01:09:51,000
It was released on July 6, 2022, by National
Geographic Documentary Films and Neon.

10
01:17:30,000 --> 01:17:36,000
It received acclaim from critics, and was nominated for Best
Documentary Feature at the 95th Academy Awards.

11
01:25:15,000 --> 01:25:21,000
The film explores themes of married couple, volcano,
interview, volcanology, archive footage.
